IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 55 to 59 -- ISSUE AND THE
-- ISSUER: notice of a defect, the purchaser for value, genuineness, defences, staleness, unauthorized
-- signatures, completion and alteration, and the warranties of those who sign. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what the Part
-- does in a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds and the provision therefore applies; FALSE
-- means only that this provision does not apply, never that the opposite holds. A rule whose result is a
-- MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within one module, a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs; a plain
-- input stands in for another section only across modules, and says so ("out of range" or "to avoid a cycle").

§ `s 55 Notice of defect; purchaser for value; defences`

§§ `s 55(1) Notice of defect`

-- The terms of the security are those stated on it and those incorporated by reference to another
-- instrument, act, statute, rule, regulation or order, to the extent the incorporated terms do not
-- conflict with the stated terms. This holds even against a purchaser for value without notice of a defect.
-- src:870 | Issue — Issuer
-- src:871 | Notice of defect
-- src:872 | 55 (1) Even against a purchaser for value without notice of a defect going to the validity of a security, the terms of the security include those stated on the security and those incorporated in it by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order to the extent that the terms so incorporated do not conflict with the stated terms, but such a reference is not of itself notice to a purchaser for value of a defect going to the validity of the security, even though the security expressly states that a person accepting it admits the notice.
@ref CBCA s 55(1) (src:870-872)
GIVEN `the term is stated on the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term is incorporated in the security by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the incorporated term conflicts with a stated term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the term is a term of the security within s 55(1)` MEANS
        `the term is stated on the security`
    OR  (    `the term is incorporated in the security by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order`
         AND (NOT `the incorporated term conflicts with a stated term`))

-- Such a reference is not of itself notice to a purchaser for value of a defect going to the validity of
-- the security, even though the security says that a person accepting it admits the notice. Whether the
-- security says so makes no difference, so no input asks. JUST FALSE when the security makes such a
-- reference; NOTHING when it does not, because s 55(1) then says nothing.
-- src:870 | Issue — Issuer
-- src:871 | Notice of defect
-- src:872 | 55 (1) Even against a purchaser for value without notice of a defect going to the validity of a security, the terms of the security include those stated on the security and those incorporated in it by reference to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order to the extent that the terms so incorporated do not conflict with the stated terms, but such a reference is not of itself notice to a purchaser for value of a defect going to the validity of the security, even though the security expressly states that a person accepting it admits the notice.
@ref CBCA s 55(1) (src:870-872)
GIVEN `the security refers to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is of itself notice to a purchaser for value of a defect going to validity within s 55(1)` MEANS
    IF `the security refers to another instrument or act, statute, rule, regulation or order`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 55(2) Purchaser for value`

-- src:873 | Purchaser for value
-- src:874 | (2) A security is valid in the hands of a purchaser for value without notice of any defect going to its validity.
@ref CBCA s 55(2) (src:873-874)
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has notice of a defect going to the validity of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the security is valid in the hands of the purchaser for value without notice within s 55(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a purchaser for value`
    AND (NOT `the person has notice of a defect going to the validity of the security`)

§§ `s 55(3) Lack of genuineness`

-- Subject to section 57, that a security is not genuine is a complete defence even against a purchaser for
-- value without notice. The exception is s 57's: an unauthorized signature that is effective in favour of a
-- purchaser. This rule calls `an unauthorized signature is effective in favour of the purchaser within s 57`
-- and takes its inputs, so the facts are stated once.
-- src:875 | Lack of genuineness
-- src:876 | (3) Subject to section 57, the fact that a security is not genuine is a complete defence even against a purchaser for value without notice.
@ref CBCA s 55(3) (src:875-876)
GIVEN `the security is not genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`lack of genuineness is a complete defence within s 55(3)` MEANS
        `the security is not genuine`
    AND (NOT `an unauthorized signature is effective in favour of the purchaser within s 57`
                 `the signature is unauthorized`
                 `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security`
                 `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority`
                 `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing`
                 `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`)

§§ `s 55(4) Ineffective defences`

-- src:877 | Ineffective defences
-- src:878 | (4) All other defences of an issuer, including non-delivery and conditional delivery of a security, are ineffective against a purchaser for value without notice of the particular defence.
@ref CBCA s 55(4) (src:877-878)
GIVEN `the defence is a defence of the issuer other than lack of genuineness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has notice of the particular defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the defence of the issuer is ineffective against the purchaser within s 55(4)` MEANS
        `the defence is a defence of the issuer other than lack of genuineness`
    AND `the person is a purchaser for value`
    AND (NOT `the person has notice of the particular defence`)

§ `s 56 Staleness as notice of defect`

-- After an event that creates a right to immediate performance of the principal obligation evidenced by a
-- security, or that sets a date on or after which a security is to be presented or surrendered for
-- redemption or exchange, a purchaser is deemed to have notice of any defect in its issue or of any defence
-- of the issuer, (a) if the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on
-- presentation or surrender, and such money or securities are available on the date set for payment or
-- exchange, and the purchaser takes the security more than one year after that date; or (b) if the purchaser
-- takes the security more than two years after the date set for presentation or surrender or the date on
-- which such performance became due. The two dates are not the same date in the text, so they are two
-- inputs; each is NOTHING when no such date was set. TRUE means s 56 deems notice. FALSE means only that
-- s 56 does not.
-- src:879 | Staleness as notice of defect
-- src:880 | 56 After an event that creates a right to immediate performance of the principal obligation evidenced by a security, or that sets a date on or after which a security is to be presented or surrendered for redemption or exchange, a purchaser is deemed to have notice of any defect in its issue or of any defence of the issuer,
-- src:881 | (a) if the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender of the security, and such money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange, and the purchaser takes the security more than one year after that date; or
-- src:882 | (b) if the purchaser takes the security more than two years after the date set for presentation or surrender or the date on which such performance became due.
@ref CBCA s 56 (src:879-882)
GIVEN `the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the purchaser takes the security` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser is deemed to have notice of a defect or defence within s 56` MEANS
        (    `the event requires the payment of money or the delivery of securities, or both, on presentation or surrender`
         AND `the money or securities are available on the date set for payment or exchange`
         AND CONSIDER `the date set for payment or exchange, if one was set`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST d THEN `the date the purchaser takes the security`
                 GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` d))
    OR  CONSIDER `the date set for presentation or surrender, or on which performance became due, if one was`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST e THEN `the date the purchaser takes the security`
            GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` e)

§ `s 57 Unauthorized signature`

-- An unauthorized signature on a security before or in the course of its issue is ineffective, except that
-- it is effective in favour of a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority if the
-- signing was done by (a) an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by
-- the issuer with the signing of the security or its immediate preparation for signing, or (b) an employee
-- of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security.
-- src:883 | Unauthorized signature
-- src:884 | 57 An unauthorized signature on a security before or in the course of its issue is ineffective, except that the signature is effective in favour of a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority, if the signing has been done by
-- src:885 | (a) an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security, or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing; or
-- src:886 | (b) an employee of the issuer or of a person referred to in paragraph (a) who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security.
@ref CBCA s 57 (src:883-886)
GIVEN `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an unauthorized signature is effective in favour of the purchaser within s 57` MEANS
        `the signature is unauthorized`
    AND `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security`
    AND `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority`
    AND (   `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing`
         OR `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`)

-- src:883 | Unauthorized signature
-- src:884 | 57 An unauthorized signature on a security before or in the course of its issue is ineffective, except that the signature is effective in favour of a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority, if the signing has been done by
-- src:885 | (a) an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security, or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing; or
-- src:886 | (b) an employee of the issuer or of a person referred to in paragraph (a) who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security.
@ref CBCA s 57 (src:883-886)
GIVEN `the signature is unauthorized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an unauthorized signature is ineffective within s 57` MEANS
        `the signature is unauthorized`
    AND `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security`
    AND (NOT `an unauthorized signature is effective in favour of the purchaser within s 57`
                 `the signature is unauthorized`
                 `the signature was made before or in the course of the issue of the security`
                 `the person claiming under it is a purchaser for value and without notice of the lack of authority`
                 `the signing was done by an authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security or of similar securities, or their immediate preparation for signing`
                 `the signing was done by an employee of the issuer or of such a person who in the ordinary course of their duties handles the security`)

§ `s 58 Completion or alteration`

§§ `s 58(1) Completion or alteration`

-- src:887 | Completion or alteration
-- src:888 | 58 (1) Where a security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer but is incomplete in any other respect,
-- src:889 | (a) any person may complete it by filling in the blanks in accordance with their authority; and
-- src:890 | (b) notwithstanding that the blanks are incorrectly filled in, the security as completed is enforceable by a purchaser who took it for value and without notice of such incorrectness.
@ref CBCA s 58(1)(a) (src:887-889)
GIVEN `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security is incomplete in some other respect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the blanks are filled in in accordance with the authority of the person completing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may complete the security by filling in the blanks within s 58(1)(a)` MEANS
        `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer`
    AND `the security is incomplete in some other respect`
    AND `the blanks are filled in in accordance with the authority of the person completing it`

-- src:887 | Completion or alteration
-- src:888 | 58 (1) Where a security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer but is incomplete in any other respect,
-- src:889 | (a) any person may complete it by filling in the blanks in accordance with their authority; and
-- src:890 | (b) notwithstanding that the blanks are incorrectly filled in, the security as completed is enforceable by a purchaser who took it for value and without notice of such incorrectness.
@ref CBCA s 58(1)(b) (src:887-890)
GIVEN `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security was incomplete in some other respect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the blanks were incorrectly filled in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enforcing it took it for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enforcing it took it without notice of the incorrectness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the security as completed is enforceable by the purchaser within s 58(1)(b)` MEANS
        `the security contains the signatures necessary for its issue or transfer`
    AND `the security was incomplete in some other respect`
    AND `the blanks were incorrectly filled in`
    AND `the person enforcing it took it for value`
    AND `the person enforcing it took it without notice of the incorrectness`

§§ `s 58(2) Enforceability`

-- src:891 | Enforceability
-- src:892 | (2) A completed security that has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently altered, remains enforceable but only according to its original terms.
@ref CBCA s 58(2) (src:891-892)
GIVEN `the security is a completed security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the security remains enforceable only according to its original terms within s 58(2)` MEANS
        `the security is a completed security`
    AND `the security has been improperly altered, even if fraudulently`

§ `s 59 Warranties of agents`

§§ `s 59(1) Warranties of agents`

-- src:893 | Warranties of agents
-- src:894 | 59 (1) A person signing a security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security warrants to a purchaser for value without notice that
-- src:895 | (a) the security is genuine;
-- src:896 | (b) the person’s acts in connection with the issue of the security are within their authority; and
-- src:897 | (c) the person has reasonable grounds for believing that the security is in the form and within the amount the issuer is authorized to issue.
@ref CBCA s 59(1) (src:893-897)
DECLARE `Warranty given on signing a security under s 59(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a warranty that the security is genuine`
    `a warranty that the signer's acts in connection with the issue of the security are within their authority`
    `a warranty that the signer has reasonable grounds for believing that the security is in the form and within the amount the issuer is authorized to issue`

-- NOTHING: the signer is not one of the persons named, or the other party is not a purchaser for value
-- without notice, so s 59(1) gives that party no warranty.
-- src:893 | Warranties of agents
-- src:894 | 59 (1) A person signing a security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security warrants to a purchaser for value without notice that
-- src:895 | (a) the security is genuine;
-- src:896 | (b) the person’s acts in connection with the issue of the security are within their authority; and
-- src:897 | (c) the person has reasonable grounds for believing that the security is in the form and within the amount the issuer is authorized to issue.
@ref CBCA s 59(1) (src:893-897)
GIVEN `the person signs the security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Warranty given on signing a security under s 59(1)`)
`the warranties the signer gives within s 59(1)` MEANS
    IF     `the person signs the security as authenticating trustee, registrar, transfer agent or other person entrusted by the issuer with the signing of the security`
       AND `the other party is a purchaser for value without notice`
    THEN JUST (LIST `a warranty that the security is genuine`,
                    `a warranty that the signer's acts in connection with the issue of the security are within their authority`,
                    `a warranty that the signer has reasonable grounds for believing that the security is in the form and within the amount the issuer is authorized to issue`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 59(2) Limitation of liability`

-- src:898 | Limitation of liability
-- src:899 | (2) Unless otherwise agreed, a person referred to in subsection (1) does not assume any further liability for the validity of a security.
@ref CBCA s 59(2) (src:898-899)
GIVEN `the person is one referred to in subsection 59(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person assumes no further liability for the validity of the security within s 59(2)` MEANS
        `the person is one referred to in subsection 59(1)`
    AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
